  {
    "id": "the-void",
    "name": "The Void",
    "kind": "between",
    "epithet": "The nothingness that lies beyond",
    "summary": "The liminal place between the planes. The void is the infinite nothingness that lies beyond  time and existence. Seldom are those who actually know of it, and amongst them many were rendered mad by the sheer ineffability of infinity.",
    "colour": "#9f6bff",
    "icon": "blur_circular",
    "glow": true,
    "iconImage": "images/planes-icons/void-symbol.svg",
    "iconScale": 134,
    "iconX": 0,
    "iconY": 0,
    "look": {
      "theme": "void",
      "textureStrength": 37
    },
    "body": "By essence the Void is something that escapes knowledge. Ancient civilizations seem to have been aware of its existence, for scholars found carvings and texts depicting it. Most scholars, even in Runebridge and the Caerotrom Athenaeum stay clear of it, for many believe it holds secrets that better be known. Some, however, see it as a mystery that requires solving. Sages of the Black Archive often share an interest in it, sometimes because of its linked to the Ophrasian and how it changed the world, others because of the unstoppable drive to know the unknowable.",
    "links": [
      "nihilium",
      "sigil-session-9"
    ]
  },
